item+ const src/oauth.rs :: CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY :: pub const CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY: &str = concat!( "default-src 'self'; ", :: Policy for the embedded editor and the public pages.  The shell is one HTML document: an inline script, an inline stylesheet, `onclick` attributes, and `style` attributes. A nonce or a hash does not cover event-handler or style attributes, so those would mean rewriting the shell. `unsafe-inline` stays for that reason. There is no `unsafe-eval`. Sign-in is a same-origin link to `/api/auth/...`, which 302s to Google or GitHub; top-level navigations are not restricted. `upgrade-insecure-requests` is added only when the browser connection is HTTPS, so a local `http://127.0.0.1` session keeps working. :: doc comment :: 768 :: 1
item+ const src/oauth.rs :: HSTS_VALUE :: pub const HSTS_VALUE: &str = "max-age=31536000"; :: One year. Matches `deploy/nginx-edit.phext.io.conf`. No `includeSubDomains`: this host is `edit.phext.io`, and a future sibling name under that host should not be pinned by accident. :: doc comment :: 756 :: 1
