item+ function src/oauth.rs :: sso :: pub fn sso(&self, headers: &HashMap<String, String>, query: &HashMap<String, String>) -> Reply { :: `GET /api/auth/sso/mutable` — the cross-site handoff to Mutable.  Layering follows the claims/submissions precedent in the servers: a signed-in account is enough; an editor's place is not required (`sso_admits` is the single predicate that decides). With a session, the reply 302s to Mutable's callback with a freshly sealed assertion. Without one, it 302s to this site's own root with this endpoint as the `next`, so the ordinary provider sign-in returns the browser here and the handoff completes — the OAuth `next` itself stays same-site throughout. Unconfigured (no SSO secret), the endpoint simply does not exist: 404. :: doc comment :: 1249 :: 1
