item+ struct src/oauth.rs :: Limiter :: pub struct Limiter { :: In-memory cap on sign-in attempts per client address, per ten minutes.  Counts OAuth start/callback and a bearer token the server rejected (the token box sends that secret as `Authorization` on the next API call). Anonymous 401s are not counted, so opening the signed-out page does not spend the budget. The address is `X-Real-IP` when nginx sets it from `$remote_addr`; otherwise the last `X-Forwarded-For` hop, which is the one a single reverse proxy appends. :: doc comment :: 834 :: 1
