item+ function src/oauth.rs :: oauth :: pub fn oauth(&self) -> &Oauth { :: Function oauth takes no inputs beyond the value it is called on, and gives back &Oauth. :: signature :: 1213 :: 0
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: open_sso_assertion :: pub fn open_sso_assertion(&self, token: &str) -> Result<SsoAssertionBody, String> { :: Open an SSO assertion under the SSO secret — the exchange endpoint is the one place this server ever takes an assertion back, and only the desktop audience's. Expiry is checked here; audience, state, and single-use are the caller's to enforce (the burn lives on the `Gate`, which owns request state). Every failure is the same error: the exchange must not say which check a forged assertion failed. :: doc comment :: 752 :: 1
