item+ function src/oauth.rs :: sso_target_for :: pub fn sso_target_for(&self, aud: &str) -> Option<&str> { :: The callback origin for an audience, or None when the audience is not allowlisted or is allowlisted but unconfigured. Mutable always has a target (its production origin is the default); Exocortexia has one only once `PHEXT_SSO_EXOCORTEXIA_URL` is set, and Wishnode only once `PHEXT_SSO_WISHNODE_URL` is. This match is the audience allowlist — an audience that is not named here can never be minted for. The desktop audience is deliberately absent: it has no fixed origin (its callback is the app's per-attempt loopback listener), so it is armed and minted on its own path (`sso_desktop_ready`, `sso_assertion_desktop`). :: doc comment :: 450 :: 1
