item+ struct src/oauth.rs :: Editors :: pub struct Editors { :: Accounts allowed to use the editor once signed in.  The list starts from `PHEXT_EDITORS` (the operator's bootstrap list) and can grow at runtime: when an editor accepts a submission, the originator's account is admitted — appended here and, when a backing file is configured (see `Gate::load_editors_file`), to that file, so the admission takes effect immediately and survives restarts. Entries sit behind a lock because admission happens through `&Gate` while other requests are reading the list. :: doc comment :: 843 :: 1
item+ struct src/oauth.rs :: Gate :: pub struct Gate { :: Access control for the editor servers: an OAuth session, or open when sign-in is not configured. :: doc comment :: 1151 :: 1
item+ struct src/oauth.rs :: Limiter :: pub struct Limiter { :: In-memory cap on sign-in attempts per client address, per ten minutes.  Counts OAuth start/callback attempts. Anonymous 401s are not counted, so opening the signed-out page does not spend the budget. The address is `X-Real-IP` when nginx sets it from `$remote_addr`; otherwise the last `X-Forwarded-For` hop, which is the one a single reverse proxy appends. :: doc comment :: 977 :: 1
